# Dual tree (`app/` + `android-app/`)

`android-app/` is a full copy of the product, not a shared module. A fix in one tree does not update the other.

## Do

- After changing a file under `app/src/`, apply the same change under `android-app/src/` (or the reverse), unless the user asked for one tree only.
- If a bake script already dual-writes (GPX maps, corners, racing lines), run that script instead of hand-copying JSON.
- Packs and `tracks.json` enforcement write `app/` only — copy the result to `android-app/` yourself. See `.cursor/skills/dual-tree-apply/SKILL.md`.

## Do not

- Leave `android-app/` stale after an `app/` logic or data fix.
- Symlink or merge the two trees.
